// TEST: GroupBy GroupKeys Inline (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3017
// ERROR-CONTAINS: inline as `group_by`'s grouping argument
// The other half of the same rule: `group_by` reads the grouping out of
// locals suffixed off a BINDING name, so an inline `group_keys(...)` has no
// name to suffix and nothing to read. Two ops, one binding between them.
//
// This used to surface as BL7001 ("code generation has no rule for
// IRGroupKeys in expression position ... this is a gap in the C++ back end,
// not an error in your program"), which was the wrong diagnosis twice over:
// it is a rule about the program, and the note invited a bug report for a
// hole nobody intends to fill.
let region = [0, 1, 0, 0, 1]
let v = [10.0, 20.0, 30.0, 40.0, 50.0]
let gv = group_by(v, group_keys(region))
let s = method_for(gv) <@> lambda(r: Array<Float64 like RaggedIdx<_>>) -> reduce(r, (+)) |> compute
// EXPECT: BL3017 -- bind the keys to a name first, then hand that name to
// `group_by`. Every passing test in this directory is spelled that way.
